<template>
    <heading>SelectProject async work</heading>
    <keywords>
        <li>SelectProject</li>
        <li>async</li>
        <li>directory picker</li>
        <li>completion command</li>
    </keywords>
    <section data-lp5-kind="explanation">
        <p><code>asyncSelectProject</code> is nested inside the <code>SelectProject</code> generator by a bundle reference. The generator starts it during priming, before yielding, so <code>showDirectoryPicker()</code> runs during the Select button's user activation.</p>
        <p>Only the picker call is inside the error handler. <code>AbortError</code> dispatches <code>ProjectPickerAborted</code>; it can mean dismissal, a restricted directory, or permission refusal. Every other picker exception is rethrown unchanged.</p>
        <p>After selection, the async function awaits <code>model.selectProject(directoryHandle)</code> to persist and install the handle, then awaits <code>model.loadProject()</code>. Only a fully loaded model produces <code>ProjectLoaded</code>. Neither the handle nor article data is carried by that command. Persistence and loading errors escape to global fatal-error handling, including errors named <code>AbortError</code>.</p>
        <p>Completion dispatch is queued, allowing the generator to suspend and be installed before it receives a command. The generator waits throughout selection and loading; it contains no <code>await</code> calls.</p>
    </section>
    <section data-lp5-kind="code">
        <name>SelectProject async work</name>
        <code><![CDATA[
async function asyncSelectProject() {
    let directoryHandle;
    try {
        directoryHandle = await window.showDirectoryPicker();
    } catch (error) {
        if (error.name !== "AbortError") throw error;
        controller.dispatch({ name: "ProjectPickerAborted", error });
        return;
    }

    await model.selectProject(directoryHandle);
    await model.loadProject();
    controller.dispatch({ name: "ProjectLoaded" });
}
]]></code>
    </section>
</template>
